<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><!--
  Keeps the AboutLibraries JSON in shrunk builds.

  `LibraryRepositoryImpl` passes `R.raw.aboutlibraries` by id, which the resource shrinker can
  see, so this should be redundant. It is here anyway because the failure it guards against is
  the worst shape available: the resource is generated by a Gradle plugin, it is only read on the
  Licenses screen, `isShrinkResources = true` applies to release only — so a regression cannot
  reproduce in a debug build — and AboutLibraries *catches* the resulting read failure and
  carries on with no data, so nothing reaches Crashlytics either. It surfaces as a screen
  claiming the licence list could not be loaded, in production, silently.

  Four lines to make that impossible is a better trade than being right about the shrinker.
-->
<resources xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools"
    tools:keep="@raw/aboutlibraries" />
